/T (Determining which classical encryption scheme is more vulnerable requires analyzing the specific cryptanalytic techniques used to break them. Substitution techniques are fundamentally more vulnerable to traditional frequency analysis attacks, whereas transposition techniques are more vulnerable to structural geometric profiling \(anagramming\).)
/E (Determining which classical encryption scheme is more vulnerable requires analyzing the specific cryptanalytic techniques used to break them. Substitution techniques are fundamentally more vulnerable to traditional frequency analysis attacks, whereas transposition techniques are more vulnerable to structural geometric profiling \(anagramming\).)
