/Title (Modern healthcare informatics systems use highly resilient embedding techniques to bind patient diagnostic data directly into medical imaging files \(such as DICOM radiographs\). To ensure this critical data survives lossy JPEG compression, scaling, or format conversions during hospital transfers, engineers implement Spread Spectrum Image Steganography \(SSIS\). By distributing the patient data across the image's high-order frequency domains, the metadata survives compression artifacts, ensuring medical personnel can always verify the patient's identity directly from the visual asset.)
/Dest [19 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1231 0 R
/Prev 1254 0 R
>>
endobj
