1338 0 obj
<<
/Title (Classical encryption methodologies are categorically segregated into two core algorithmic philosophies: Substitution Techniques and Transposition Techniques. While substitution alters the actual identity of characters while preserving their geometric positions within the message string, transposition retains the exact original identities of the cleartext characters but systematically scrambles and permutes their spatial and sequential alignment. These two opposing approaches represent the early paradigms of structural confusion and diffusion, which are critical for obscuring systematic trends within ciphertext streams.)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1327 0 R
/First 1350 0 R
/Last 1351 0 R
/Count -2
>>
endobj
1339 0 obj
<<
/Title <8020446174612053747275637475726520496D706163743A>
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1307 0 R
